Title
Binary Tree Representation of a Propositional Formula

Aim
Read a formula in propositional-calculus style and create its binary tree representation. Determine the time and space complexity of the function.

Parameters
Input: formula tokens/operators. Output: binary expression tree. For a token-based construction, time is O(n) and space is O(n), where n is the number of tokens.

Procedure
1. Tokenize the formula.
2. Identify operands and binary operators.
3. Build nodes for operands.
4. Attach left and right subtrees according to the operator structure.
5. Display the tree using inorder/preorder traversal.
6. State complexity as O(n) for a linear construction.

Program

class Node:
    def __init__(self, value, left=None, right=None):
        self.value = value
        self.left = left
        self.right = right

# Example formula: (A AND B) OR C
root = Node("OR",
            Node("AND", Node("A"), Node("B")),
            Node("C"))

def preorder(root):
    if root:
        print(root.value, end=" ")
        preorder(root.left)
        preorder(root.right)

print("Binary tree preorder:")
preorder(root)
print("\nTime complexity: O(n)")
print("Space complexity: O(n)")
